1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,080
The Washing Machine

2
00:00:05,759 --> 00:00:07,160
Look at that, Simka!

3
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:09,720
They're showing Titanic on the television!

4
00:00:11,519 --> 00:00:14,040
Hey, Nolik! That's not a television!

5
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:16,120
That's a machine for washing laundry!

6
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:17,359
No way!

7
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:20,440
Yeah, it's just a plain old washing machine, Nolik, don't you know?

8
00:00:20,519 --> 00:00:22,320
Uh-uh! Tell me about it!

9
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:24,839
You're such a great explainer!

10
00:00:24,839 --> 00:00:30,199
Inside of a washing machine is a big drum.

11
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:35,320
People put their dirty laundry in there and add a special kind of soap called detergent.

12
00:00:35,519 --> 00:00:39,439
When they turn the washing machine on, the drum fills with water,

13
00:00:39,519 --> 00:00:42,359
and then the motor starts to spin the drum.

14
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,480
That makes the laundry rub together,

15
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:49,439
forcing the soapy water in and the dirt out to make your clothes clean.

16
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:54,200
After that, all that's left is to get out the water by spinning the drum really fast

17
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:56,560
and sending the water down the drain.

18
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:00,720
Oh, thanks a lot, Simka!

19
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:02,120
I always wondered,

20
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:05,480
why would you want to put laundry inside a television?

21
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:07,560
Are you joking with me?

22
00:01:07,719 --> 00:01:08,439
Uh-huh!

23
00:01:09,359 --> 00:01:11,000
Oh, I'll show you a funny joke!

24
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,240
Get over here!

25
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:16,200
Shhh! It's Tom Thomas' mother!

26
00:01:20,439 --> 00:01:22,159
She's got headphones on, we're safe.

27
00:01:22,159 --> 00:01:24,479
She doesn't hear anything except the music.

28
00:01:29,479 --> 00:01:31,560
Now she'll come back, add the soap,

29
00:01:31,759 --> 00:01:33,159
turn on her television,

30
00:01:33,239 --> 00:01:35,479
and watch the second part of the movie.

31
00:01:35,759 --> 00:01:37,280
Again with the jokes!

32
00:01:37,399 --> 00:01:39,759
This time I'm really gonna let you have it!

33
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,159
Whoa!

34
00:01:45,479 --> 00:01:47,599
Nolik, just do what I say.

35
00:01:47,719 --> 00:01:49,319
I came up with a plan.

36
00:01:49,439 --> 00:01:50,679
What's your plan?

37
00:01:50,759 --> 00:01:51,679
To run away!

38
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,500
Oh, oh, oh!

39
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:00,900
Who's here?

40
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,500
Hello?

41
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,500
Food.

42
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:34,800
There are a lot of things to keep in mind with a washing machine to use it right.

43
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,719
For example, do you know what can happen if you wash red and white shirts together?

44
00:02:38,719 --> 00:02:42,120
Well, the white one might just turn pink!

45
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,120
No!

46
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:47,139
It's not because it's embarrassed, but because some of the color from the red shirt happened

47
00:02:47,139 --> 00:02:48,900
to get onto the white one.

48
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:53,300
Another important thing to remember is to empty your pockets before you wash your clothes.

49
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:56,939
Things like keys, nails, and chewing gum might not only ruin your clothes,

50
00:02:56,939 --> 00:02:59,180
but they can destroy the washer too.

51
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,300
And this isn't only about little stuff.

52
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,980
Big things like music players and mobile phones

53
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:06,620
have managed to find their way into the washing machine.

54
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:10,740
Oh, sure, these things look nice and clean after a good washing,

55
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:13,379
but they certainly don't seem to want to work anymore.

56
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:17,620
And never ever put a pet inside of a washing machine.

57
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:19,939
That's just no place for a living thing!

58
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:31,780
You know what, Simka?

59
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:34,659
I've never been laundered in my entire life!

60
00:03:34,819 --> 00:03:37,219
We'd better get out of here, Nolik, right now!

61
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,900
And the faster the better!

62
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:50,960
Come on. Let's get going.

63
00:03:51,539 --> 00:03:53,000
And what about Chewsocka?

64
00:03:53,219 --> 00:03:54,400
What about Chewsocka?

65
00:03:54,759 --> 00:03:56,360
Let her get washed up a little in there.

66
00:03:56,659 --> 00:03:57,819
Maybe it'll make her nicer.

67
00:03:58,080 --> 00:03:59,860
But she could drown the poor thing.

68
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:04,599
Eep!

69
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:09,040
I don't think we can do this alone.

70
00:04:09,379 --> 00:04:11,140
We should get help from Tom Thomas' mother.

71
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,680
One, two, stop!

72
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,079
One… What?

73
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:19,079
She moved out of the way!

74
00:04:27,079 --> 00:04:28,079
And three!

75
00:04:32,079 --> 00:04:33,079
Pull it!

76
00:04:37,079 --> 00:04:39,079
Huh? What is that?

77
00:04:40,079 --> 00:04:41,079
Oh my goodness!

78
00:04:41,079 --> 00:04:41,719
Goodness!

79
00:04:45,359 --> 00:04:47,359
Oh, my sweet little baby!

80
00:04:47,439 --> 00:04:48,800
How did you get in there?

81
00:04:48,919 --> 00:04:51,599
You wait right here in the tub and I'll go get you a towel.

82
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:55,599
So, you wild little beast!

83
00:04:55,919 --> 00:04:57,719
Looks like we saved your life!

84
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,159
We're friends now?

85
00:05:01,159 --> 00:05:03,879
Nolik, it sure doesn't look like she wants to be our friend.

86
00:05:03,959 --> 00:05:05,159
So what do we do now?

87
00:05:05,279 --> 00:05:07,599
Same old plan! Run!

